body:
Bumps [i18next](https://github.com/i18next/i18next) from 26.5.11 to 27.0.0.
<details>
<summary>Release notes</summary>
<p><em>Sourced from <a href="https://github.com/i18next/i18next/releases">i18next's releases</a>.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<h2>v27.0.0</h2>
<p><strong>This is a major breaking release.</strong> It changes defaults that most setups had to override, gives every instance its own logger and post-processors, refuses language codes that look like markup or paths, and removes options that were broken or had no effect. 26.7 warned in debug mode about most of the runtime changes. The <a href="https://www.i18next.com/misc/migration-guide#v26.x.x-to-v27.0.0">migration guide</a> has the details; to keep the v26 behavior where an option exists:</p>
<pre lang="js"><code>i18next.init({
  fallbackLng: 'dev', // or better your source language: there is no implicit 'dev' any more
  returnEmptyString: true, // an empty translation is a translation again
  cleanCode: false, // keep codes without a region as they are ('EN' stays 'EN')
});
</code></pre>
<pre lang="ts"><code>declare module 'i18next' {
  interface CustomTypeOptions {
    strictInterpolationChecks: false;
    returnEmptyString: true;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<h3>Changed defaults</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>fallbackLng</code> defaults to <code>false</code> instead of <code>['dev']</code>. Without a <code>fallbackLng</code>, i18next no longer requests <code>dev</code> from the backend (<code>/locales/dev/translation.json</code> with i18next-http-backend), and <code>saveMissing</code> sends missing keys for the current language instead of <code>dev</code>. With <code>supportedLngs</code> and no <code>fallbackLng</code>, an unsupported language leaves <code>language</code> and <code>languages</code> unset, as <code>fallbackLng: false</code> already did. Set <code>fallbackLng</code> to your main language, or to <code>'dev'</code> for the previous behavior.</li>
<li><code>returnEmptyString</code> defaults to <code>false</code>: an empty translation falls back like a missing value (to the fallback language, the default value or the key), as <code>null</code> already does. i18next-cli writes <code>''</code> for untranslated keys in the other languages, which now fall back instead of rendering blank. An explicit <code>''</code> default from code still counts: <code>t('key', '')</code> and <code>t('key', { defaultValue: '' })</code> return <code>''</code>. Set <code>returnEmptyString: true</code> (in <code>init()</code> and in <code>CustomTypeOptions</code>) if an empty translation is meant to render nothing, for example for a Locize project with &quot;preserve empty strings&quot; on.</li>
<li>Language codes without a region get their canonical casing, as codes with one already did: <code>'EN'</code> becomes <code>'en'</code>. Only the casing changes: aliases like <code>tl</code>, <code>iw</code> or <code>eng</code> stay as they are (<code>'TL'</code> becomes <code>'tl'</code>), and so do codes that are not BCP 4

